  {
   "id": "lM_XoVmwBAAJ",
   "from": "Stephen Buckland",
   "author": "1fb54f491646a589",
   "date": "2023-12-22T11:33:34Z",
   "subject": "Re: {Suspected Spam} [distance-sampling] Error message",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Adding to Eric’s comments, as he notes, movement is likely to be a major issue, unless you had a protocol to deal with this. Movement independent of the observer generates too many detections close to the line unless it is slow relative to observer\r\n speed (if for example you were using a vehicle or drone). However, it would be unlikely to generate the spike at zero that your data show. That might occur if for example your transects were tracks through forest, and kites were often seen crossing the track\r\n ahead of the observer. It might also occur if observers were not trained to get good estimates of distance from the line, and often recorded birds that were ahead of them as on the line. Another possibility is that<span>  missing distance estimates were recorded\r\n as zeros.</span><span></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><span><br>\r\n</span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><span>Steve Buckland </span></div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr\"></div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr\"></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"font-size:11pt\" color=\"#000000\"><b>From:</b> &#39;Eric Rexstad&#39; via distance-sampling &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Friday, December 22, 2023 9:45:26 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> Alan Omar Bermúdez Cavero &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bec...@gmail.com</a>&gt;; <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Re: {Suspected Spam} [distance-sampling] Error message</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nAlan</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nSeveral issues associated with your question.</div>\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type:disc\">\r\n<li style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nFirst the error message. Your data file contains five values for <code>Region.Label</code>​. The software is checking that the transect length associated with transects within each\r\n<code>Region.Label</code>​ are the same. That is not the case with your data, because you have the 2022 and 2023 data within the same\r\n<code>Region.Label</code>​. For example, Transect 1 in Region <code>Mota C.</code>​ has\r\n<code>Effort=5</code>​ for 2022, but the same transect has <code>Effort=3.8</code>​ for 2023.</div>\r\n</li><ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\">\r\n<li style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Solution: Recast your data such that the Regions are\r\n<code>Mota22</code>​, <code>Mota23</code>​, <code>Belmonte22</code>​, <code>Belmonte23</code>​, etc. This will solve your error message, but it will highlight that there are unlikely to be sufficient detections to support unique detection function models for\r\n each of your location x season combinations.</span></li><li style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Number of detections by location (ignoring year):</span></li><ul style=\"list-style-type:square\">\r\n<li style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">MOTAC=20, BELMONTE=8, QUERO=51, LONGAR=28, P.MUNOZ=16</span></li><li style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">this suggests you will struggle to produce defensible estimates by location (ignoring year) without the use of location as\r\n a covariate</span></li><li style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">when you truncate to a reasonable distance, e.g. 100m, the 123 total detections is reduced to ~80<br>\r\n</span></li></ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Distribution of detection distances will make it difficult to fit a detection function model. Half-normal key function models\r\n will lack fit and hazard rate key function models will predict unrealistically large estimates of density<br>\r\n</span></li><ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\">\r\n<li style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Of the 123 detections in the data set, over 1/3 of the detections are at distances &lt;10m</span></li><li style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><img width=\"357\" height=\"390\" size=\"4741\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/4b059a1d7cf94/Rplot07.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" style=\"width:357px;min-height:390px\"><br>\r\n</span></li></ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n<div></div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nFinally, animal movement cause bias in density estimates. If the red kites were detected in flight, this might cause the spike in detections at small distances leading to modelling difficulties. Best to detect animals before they detect you.</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Aptos,Aptos_EmbeddedFont,Aptos_MSFontService,Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\nCode used to develop above. Note, estimates from this analysis are unreliable for reasons described in the email:</div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">library(readxl)</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">dat &lt;- read_excel(&quot;c:/users/erexs/downloads/RedKite.xlsx&quot;)</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">hist(dat$distance, xlim=c(0,400), nc=80)</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">sum(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471948817000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jYBOHOndHsDlrldiNJT02\">is.na</a>(dat$distance) &amp; dat$Region.Label==&quot;MOTA C.&quot;)</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">sum(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471948817000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jYBOHOndHsDlrldiNJT02\">is.na</a>(dat$distance) &amp; dat$Region.Label==&quot;BELMONTE&quot;)</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">sum(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471948817000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jYBOHOndHsDlrldiNJT02\">is.na</a>(dat$distance) &amp; dat$Region.Label==&quot;QUERO&quot;)</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">sum(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471948817000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jYBOHOndHsDlrldiNJT02\">is.na</a>(dat$distance) &amp; dat$Region.Label==&quot;LONGAR&quot;)</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">sum(!<a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792471948817000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0jYBOHOndHsDlrldiNJT02\">is.na</a>(dat$distance) &amp; dat$Region.Label==&quot;P.MUNOZ&quot;)</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"># combine location and year into a single variable for Region.Label</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">dat$Region.Label &lt;- paste0(dat$Region.Label, dat$season)</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">co &lt;- convert_units(&quot;meter&quot;, &quot;kilometer&quot;, &quot;square kilometer&quot;)</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">simple &lt;- ds(dat, key=&quot;hn&quot;, adjustment = &quot;cos&quot;, convert_units = co, truncation = 100)</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">gof_ds(simple)</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">summary(simple)</span></div>\r\n<div><span style=\"font-family:Consolas,Courier,monospace;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">plot(simple, nc=20)</span></div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><b>From:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Alan Omar Bermúdez Cavero &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bec...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> 22 December 2023 07:56<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> {Suspected Spam} [distance-sampling] Error message</span>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">Hi everyone,</div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">I am working with the red kite. Two visits were made. To carry out the analysis, I have been guided by the online course (Chapter 7, CDS), when I want to make the models I get the following message:</div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:13.5pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;color:blue\">&gt; model1 &lt;- ds(mreal, key=&quot;hn&quot;, adjustment=NULL, convert_units = conversion)</span></div>\r\n<pre style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;border-width:medium;border-style:none;border-color:currentcolor\"><div style=\"direction:ltr;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in checkdata(data, region_table, sample_table, obs_table, formula) : \r\n  A sample has a non-unique &quot;Effort&quot;, check data!</span></div></pre>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\">To estimate density and abundance by location and season (winter 2022 and 2023), is post-stratification appropriate?</div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Any help is greatly appreciated!!</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Best.</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:tahoma,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">PS. Attached to database</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(128,128,128)\">--------------------------------------------</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(128,128,128)\"><b>Alan Omar Bermúdez Cavero</b></span></div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial;color:rgb(128,128,128)\">RENACYT: P0011859</span></div>\r\n<div style=\"direction:ltr;font-family:Arial;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105)\">Phone: <a href=\"tel:+51%20943%20825%20461\" value=\"+51943825461\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">(+51) 943825461</a></span></div>\r\n--<br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;distance-sampling&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">\r\ndistance-sampl...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/CANM%3D676GG%3D_TYD2UHtn-0SPcUqPwuPN0YOQpd_-5hCeFF4aQjA%40mail.gmail.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/CANM%253D676GG%253D_TYD2UHtn-0SPcUqPwuPN0YOQpd_-5hCeFF4aQjA%2540mail.gmail.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_so